# Brain + session commands

This workspace has a local brain and Claudify slash-command set. Cursor CLI (`agent`) and the IDE agent must use them.

## When user says start, /start, continue, or opens a fresh session

Follow `.cursor/commands/start.md`. That wraps `.claude/commands/start.md` and then reads the brain stack.

## Sources of truth

| Need | File |
|---|---|
| Workspace invariants, read order | `AGENTS.md` |
| How to work | `documentation/agent-context/WORKING_AGREEMENT.md` |
| What is in focus now | `brain/CURRENT_STATE.local.md` |
| Task detail | `Task Board.md` |
| Command catalog | `.claude/command-index.md` |
| Command procedures | `.claude/commands/{name}.md` |
| Cursor slash wrappers | `.cursor/commands/{name}.md` (`start`, `sync`, `wrap-up`) |
| Website WCNC handoff | `brain/archives/chats/SESSION_HANDOFF.md` |

Ignore `documentation/passenger_link_devlogs/` as current product state.

## Other rituals

- `/sync` → `.cursor/commands/sync.md`
- `/wrap-up` → `.cursor/commands/wrap-up.md`
- `/audit`, `/safe-clear`, `/unstick` → read `.claude/commands/` for that name and self-execute when tools allow

Do not duplicate these files. Execute the linked procedure.
